o Donis novotná from an Bona wants to  know can memories be intentionally  erased it sounds like science fiction  and has inspired movie plots since the  early days of film but today researchers  are closer to making it a reality still  memory loss is a dreaded affliction many  elderly people suffer from Alzheimer's  and other forms of dementia so why would  anyone voluntarily choose to wipe out  their memories memory erasure could help  people suffering from depression or  post-traumatic stress disorder mental  conditions that can trigger physical  symptoms in cases where patients are  plagued by intrusive uncontrollable  negative thoughts psychologists might  wish the brain were equipped with an  erase button but it's not that simple  even if researchers have found a  promising drug that freed mice from  trauma scientists gave electrical shocks  to mice while playing a piercing sound  later the mice associated the sound with  the painful stimulus and would freeze in  shock whenever they heard it but with  drug therapy the rodents stopped  freezing when they heard the traumatic  sound  [Music]  researchers hope to develop therapies  that relieve the brain from emotions  associated with specific memories but  they won't be able to wipe out memory  and that's just as well because memories  play a vital role guarding us against  making the same mistake twice  you
 

